verdicts.note:
The hazard is real but described slightly wrong, and the fix as written does not work.

Mechanism: app_close_win sets I_STATE 1->2 and, for a record with a worker (I_TASK != 0xFF), only wm_hides (instance.inc:1662-1667,1693-1694). The worker's next OSAPI_TASK_ALIVE goes to .die, then inst_task_die, on its own slice (instance.inc:2212-2220,1929-1947). The window is already hidden, so wm_destroy banks an EMPTY rect (wm.inc:3054-3060) and wm_paint_dmg takes .chrome (wm.inc:5276-5281): wm_dock_under and menu_draw_bar. Another package's W_PAINT is reached only through wm_dock_under -> wm_dmg_wins, for windows over the dock (wm.inc:5526-5555), or through wm_destroy_seg on a still-visible unbound window. Still, dock_paint/menu_draw_bar/font_run under kent_bp frames clearly exceed Bounce's 128-byte class (bounce.asm:32) less its 64-byte floor. Overflow is plausible but unmeasured. The DESK.DRV half is real, and mod.inc:880-886 itself admits the worker drop can race the UI task's lock-free DKD_HOVER far call (ui.inc:1006-1012); the cli only prevents a torn slot.

The fix fails as stated. A posted wm_clreq reaches ui.inc .cl_slot -> app_close_win, whose `cmp byte [di+I_STATE],1 / jne .hide` (instance.inc:1662-1663) sends a record already at I_STATE 2 to .hide again, so no teardown runs and the record, region and dock tile leak. The fix must:
(a) give the posted close a teardown entry that accepts I_STATE 2 with I_TASK = 0xFF, not reuse app_close_win as is;
(b) task_exit WITHOUT the release byte (inst_task_die passes BX = DI, the I_STATE byte, at instance.inc:1946-1947, which would free the record early);
(c) add a new reap mechanism for windowless worker records, since wm_clreq is per window slot;
(d) cover kern_mega's fault-kill path, which also jumps to inst_task_die (mega.inc:2715-2721) with a still-live, visible record.
The byte estimate of +15..+30 is likely low once (a)-(c) are included.
